---
description: Before writing any plan, run the design-decision checkpoint
alwaysApply: true
---

When planning (Plan mode, or any request to design, architect, or plan something
non-trivial), do NOT write the plan or make architectural choices silently.

First use the `design-decisions` skill: thoroughly identify significant design
decisions, check which are settled, and ask the user to choose the open ones.
Present the checkpoint in the skill's condensed format. Only draft the plan
after those are answered.

Skip the checkpoint for small, local changes (a bug fix, a rename, a single
function, a typo, a config tweak).
